<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd">
<!--#include file="helpVar.asp"-->
<!--#include file="..\appletsVersion.asp"-->
<%
   Dim gsStatus
   Dim goScopeIpc
   
   gsStatus = Request.QueryString("status")
   
   If (gsStatus = "1") Then
      Set goScopeIpc = CreateObject("infiniiVisionWebCom.ScopeIpc")
      goScopeIpc.RestartRemoteFp
   End If
%>
<HTML>
<HEAD>
   <TITLE>Help Remote Front Panel </TITLE>
   <META content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type">
   <LINK href="helpStyle.css" rel="stylesheet" title="WebEnabled" type="text/css">

   <SCRIPT language="JavaScript" type="text/javascript">
      <!--      hide
      function openBrowserWindow(url)
      {
         window.open(url, 'out', 'toolbar=yes,location=yes,menubar=yes,scrollbars=yes, resizable=yes,width=640,height=400,screenX=150,screenY=150');
      }

      function applyClick(formObj)
      {
         if (confirm("Are you sure you want to restart the remote front panel server? " + "(If you click OK, all remote front panel connections to this oscilloscope will be closed)"))
         {
            return true;
         }
         else
         {
            return false;
         }
      }
      -->
   </SCRIPT>

</HEAD>
<BODY onload="document.reset.ContinueOn.value = 'False';">
   <TABLE border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
      <!-- Begin logos row - middle logo is instrument specific -->
      <TR bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
         <TD bgcolor="#FFFFFF" height="60" valign="MIDDLE" width="230">
            <IMG alt="Agilent" border="0" height="60" src="../image/agilent.gif" width="230">
         </TD>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" height="60" valign="top">
            <IMG alt="" src="../image/instrumentBanner.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
      <!-- End logos row -->
      <TR>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" colspan="2">
            <IMG alt="" height="2" src="../image/filltrans.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
   </TABLE>
   <H1>
      Remote Front Panel Help</H1>
   <P>
      The <B>Remote Front Panel</B> allows you to control with your
      <%=sModel%>
      &nbsp;oscilloscope front panel remotely using a mouse and keyboard.
   </P>
   <H1>
      Remote Front Panel Frequently Asked Questions
   </H1>
   <H2>
      Why don't I see the remote front panel?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         The remote front panel requires Sun Java Runtime Standard Edition version <%=(gsJREVersion + " ")%>
         or greater. To download directly, go to <A href="#" onclick="openBrowserWindow('http://www.java.com/')"
            onmouseout="window.status=''; return true;" onmouseover="window.status='www.java.com'; return true;">
            http://www.java.com</A>.
         <BR>
         <BR>
         If you still don't see the remote front panel, make sure java is enabled in your
         browser and your security settings allow java applets to run.
      </DD>
   </DL>
   <H2>
      Why does the remote front panel occasionally not display?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         If the remote front panel window doesn't display, and there are no error messages
         then press the "Restart Remote Front Panel Server" button below. This will restart
         the server running in the oscilloscope.
         <BR>
         <BR>
         <CENTER>
            <FORM method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data" name="reset" onsubmit="return applyClick(this.form);"
            accept="TEXT/PLAIN" action="helpRemoteFrontPanel.asp?status=1">
            <INPUT name="restartServer" onmouseout="window.status=''; return true;"
               onmouseover="window.status='Restart Remote Front Panel Server'; return true;"
               type="SUBMIT" value="Restart Remote Front Panel Server">
            </FORM>
         </CENTER>
      </DD>
   </DL>
   <H2>
      Can I access the remote front panel through a firewall?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         No, you can only access the remote front panel when both the oscilloscope and the
         remote front panel display are within a firewall.</DD>
   </DL>
   <H2>
      The Cut/Copy/Paste does not work in the remote front panel window?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         The remote front panel window is not a standard Microsoft window. It is more like
         a movie&nbsp; The Cut/Copy/Paste functions will not work.</DD>
   </DL>
   <H2>
      How do I Copy/Paste the remote front panel window?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         There are two ways to copy the remote front panel window. Press Ctrl+Alt+PrintScreen
         or select the Get Image button from your oscilloscope's home page.</DD>
   </DL>
   <H2>
      How is the remote front panel implemented?</H2>
   <DL>
      <DD>
         The remote front panel is implemented using RealVNC.</DD>
   </DL>
   <BR>
   <P>
      VNC Viewer Free Edition</P>
   <P>
      Copyright (C) 2002-2005 RealVNC Ltd.</P>
   <P>
      See <A href="#" onclick="openBrowserWindow('http://www.realvnc.com/')" onmouseout="window.status=''; return true;"
         onmouseover="window.status='www.realvnc.com'; return true;">http://www.realvnc.com</A>&nbsp;for
      information on VNC.</P>
</BODY>
</HTML>
